    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\n1.18.4\n\n### Commit Hash\n\ne7878b6b689e7df71b93876d5fc59775756c4c76\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.22\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox 1.18.4\n2. Have atox(or some other app) running on Android.\n3. Send a 5000 byte message FROM atox user on Android TO qTox user on Desktop\n    AND/OR FROM qTox user on Desktop to atox user on Android.\n4. You'll see that qTox will split the message and send 4 messages of 1371 bytes , 1371 bytes , 1371 bytes and 887 bytes.\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nMessages being split every 1371 bytes.\n\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nIncoming and Outgoing message should not be split regardless of message size. Only send 1 full message(regardless of size), as I intended.\n\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows/Android\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
